image_cache: say what became of a download, absent apart from transient

download_static_image caught every exception and logged it at debug, so a
caller learned nothing but that the file was not there. A caller that
fetches a whole store's images -- ROCKNIX's image pass, which runs at the
end of every scan and top-up -- could not tell an image the server does not
have from one that did not come this time, and one badge the server never
had (a 404) failed every pass for good.

It now returns what became of the image: "cached" (there already, or
fetched whole), "absent" (the server answered 404 or 410) or "transient"
(anything else: a timeout, a 5xx, a refused connection, a short or damaged
body), and an image it did not cache is logged at info with that class,
the URL and the HTTP status. Nothing is raised, as before; callers that
ignore the return value -- the service's own pool -- are unchanged.

Written for ROCKNIX (fork issue maxengel/rocknix#307, PL-060's
follow-up). Offered upstream as-is.

--- a/linux/raofflineproxy/image_cache.py
+++ b/linux/raofflineproxy/image_cache.py
